description:
An image is described by a pointer to its top-left pixel, its size and its **stride** (pixels from the start of one row to the start of the next):

```cpp
struct View
{
    std::uint32_t* pixels;
    int width;
    int height;
    int stride;
};

std::uint32_t* pixelAt(View v, int x, int y);
View subView(View v, int x, int y, int w, int h);
void fillRect(View v, int x, int y, int w, int h, std::uint32_t colour);
```

- **pixelAt** returns a pointer to pixel `(x, y)`, or `nullptr` if it is outside the view.
- **subView** returns a view of the rectangle `x, y, w, h` inside `v`, sharing `v`'s memory. The rectangle is first **clipped** to `v`. If nothing is left, it returns `{ nullptr, 0, 0, v.stride }`.
- **fillRect** sets every pixel of the rectangle (clipped to the view) to `colour`. Pixels outside the view, including the padding at the end of each row, must not be touched.

